1
00:03:41,538 --> 00:03:47,538
Find your place in the universe.

2
00:07:23,076 --> 00:07:29,076
Treasure Planet is a science fiction, adventure,
animation film directed by Ron Clements.

3
00:11:04,615 --> 00:11:10,615
When space galleon cabin boy Jim Hawkins discovers a map to an intergalactic "loot of a thousand worlds," a cyborg cook
named John Silver teaches him to battle supernovas and space storms on their journey to find treasure.

4
00:14:46,153 --> 00:14:52,153
Jim Hawkins (voice), played by Joseph Gordon-Levitt.

5
00:18:27,692 --> 00:18:33,692
John Silver (voice), played by Brian Murray.

6
00:22:09,230 --> 00:22:15,230
Captain Amelia (voice), played by Emma Thompson.

7
00:25:50,769 --> 00:25:56,769
Doctor Doppler (voice), played by David Hyde Pierce.

8
00:29:32,307 --> 00:29:38,307
B.E.N. (voice), played by Martin Short.

9
00:33:13,846 --> 00:33:19,846
Morph (voice), played by Dane A. Davis.

10
00:36:55,384 --> 00:37:01,384
Treasure Planet is a 2002 American animated science fiction adventure film directed by John
Musker and Ron Clements and written by Musker, Clements and Rob Edwards.

11
00:40:36,923 --> 00:40:42,923
Produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation, it is a science fiction adaptation of Robert Louis Stevenson's novel Treasure Island
(1883) and the third Disney adaptation of the novel, following Treasure Island (1950) and Muppet Treasure Island (1996).

12
00:44:18,461 --> 00:44:24,461
In the film's setting, spaceships are powered by solar sails and resemble the
18th-century sailing vessels of the original Treasure Island.

13
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The film features the voices of Joseph Gordon-Levitt, Brian Murray, David Hyde Pierce, Martin Short,  Roscoe Lee
Browne, Emma Thompson, Michael Wincott, Laurie Metcalf, and Patrick McGoohan in his final role.

14
00:51:41,538 --> 00:51:47,538
The musical score was composed by James Newton Howard, with
songs written and performed by John Rzeznik.

15
00:55:23,076 --> 00:55:29,076
Clements and Musker pitched the concept for the film during
production of The Little Mermaid (1989).

16
00:59:04,615 --> 00:59:10,615
Development began after they finished their work on Hercules (1997).

17
01:02:46,153 --> 01:02:52,153
It employs a novel technique of hand-drawn 2D traditional
animation set atop 3D computer animation.

18
01:06:27,692 --> 01:06:33,692
With a budget of $140 million, it is the most expensive
traditionally animated film to date.

19
01:10:09,230 --> 01:10:15,230
Treasure Planet premiered in Paris on November 6, 2002, and was released in
the United States on November 27 by Walt Disney Pictures.

20
01:13:50,769 --> 01:13:56,769
It was the first film to be released
simultaneously in regular and IMAX theaters.

21
01:17:32,307 --> 01:17:38,307
The film was a box-office failure, earning $109 million
worldwide against a budget of $140 million.

22
01:21:13,846 --> 01:21:19,846
It received generally positive reviews from critics and was nominated
for Best Animated Feature at the 75th Academy Awards.

23
01:24:55,384 --> 01:25:01,384
The film has since gained a cult following.

24
01:28:36,923 --> 01:28:42,923
The film explores themes of mutiny, space marine,
based on novel or book, cyborg, map.

25
01:32:18,461 --> 01:32:24,461
The tone is thought_provoking.
